1.\n\nThe continuation record identifies `generate_tests()` as the failing step, and `logs/org.apache.curator:curator-client:5.0.0/improve-library-coverage/pi-generation-2026-10-01T10-58-23-251308Z.log` ends during an unfinished inspection command. Native verification initially found one failing `ClassPathTest` (`33/34` tests passed); the preserved repair removed that test and added missing `FinalizableReference.finalizeReferent()` metadata, after which all 33 ordinary native tests passed. However, the exact trace-enabled run still exits during JUnit discovery with `StackOverflowError`, although Gradle reports success because the task ignores the binary exit code. See:\n\n- `logs/org.apache.curator:curator-client:5.0.0/native-test-verify/cycle-0-test-2026-10-01T11-24-37-603781Z.log`\n- `logs/org.apache.curator:curator-client:5.0.0/native-test-verify/cycle-0-runNativeTraceImage-2026-10-01T11-27-13-787208Z.log`\n- `logs/org.apache.curator:curator-client:5.0.0/native-test-verify/pi.log`\n\nThe generated dynamic-access report reached `99/123` calls (`80.49%`), but publication metrics were not finalized and the committed `stats.json` remains stale at `2/123`.\n\nManual next steps:\n\n1. Reproduce and resolve or isolate the trace-enabled JUnit discovery `StackOverflowError`, confirming the trace binary’s actual exit status.\n2. Review the generated tests and metadata, including the removed `ClassPathTest` and reported test-package condition warnings, then rerun the coordinate’s metadata and native-test gates.\n3. Regenerate dynamic-access coverage, library statistics, and execution metrics before publication.", "textSignature": "{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_06df6eafe9122a20016abe4d2d46c887d2b6181134f03cfe46\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}], "api": "openai-codex-responses", "provider": "openai-codex", "model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "usage": {"input": 6475, "output": 1007, "cacheRead": 191104, "cacheWrite": 0, "reasoning": 516, "totalTokens": 198586, "cost": {"input": 0.0259, "output": 0